
  <sn><md>### Complete Regex Learning Path: From Basic to Advanced

+++ #### Foundations &amp; Literals

- What regex is and isn't (pattern matching vs. parsing)
- Regex engines and flavors (PCRE, JavaScript, Python `re`, RE2, POSIX)
- Literal characters and case sensitivity
- The dot `.` (any character except newline)
- Escaping special characters (`\.`, `\*`, `\\`)
- How to test regex (regex101, debuggex, language REPLs)

**Goal:** Match exact strings and understand the concept of metacharacters.

+++

+++ #### Character Classes

- `[abc]` — character sets
- Ranges `[a-z]`, `[0-9]`, `[A-Za-z]`
- Negation `[^abc]`
- Predefined classes: `\d`, `\w`, `\s` (and their negations `\D`, `\W`, `\S`)
- POSIX classes (`[:alpha:]`, `[:digit:]`) — where they apply
- Inside vs. outside brackets: metacharacter behavior
- Escaping inside character classes

**Goal:** Match "any of these characters" patterns.

+++

+++ #### Quantifiers &amp; Repetition

- `*` (0 or more), `+` (1 or more), `?` (0 or 1)
- Exact `{n}`, range `{n,m}`, minimum `{n,}`
- Greedy vs. lazy (`*?`, `+?`, `{n,m}?`)
- Possessive quantifiers (`*+`, `++`) — PCRE/Java
- Catastrophic backtracking (intro)

**Goal:** Control how many times something repeats.

+++

+++ #### Anchors &amp; Boundaries

- `^` and `$` (start/end of line)
- `\A`, `\z`, `\Z` (string anchors — flavor-specific)
- `\b` and `\B` (word boundaries)
- Multiline mode (`m` flag)
- `\G` (end of previous match)

**Goal:** Anchor matches to positions.

+++

+++ #### Groups &amp; Capturing

- Capturing groups `(...)`
- Backreferences `\1`, `\2`
- Named groups `(?<name>...)` / `(?P<name>...)`
- Non-capturing groups `(?:...)`
- Nested groups and numbering rules
- Alternation `|` and how it interacts with groups

**Goal:** Extract and reuse parts of matches.

+++

+++ #### Lookarounds

- Positive lookahead `(?=...)`
- Negative lookahead `(?!...)`
- Positive lookbehind `(?&lt;=...)`
- Negative lookbehind `(?<!--...)`
- Variable-length lookbehind (PCRE, .NET, JS newer)
- Lookaround nesting and combining

**Goal:** Assert context without consuming it.

+++

+++ #### Flags & Modes

- `i` (case-insensitive), `m` (multiline), `s` (dotall), `x` (extended/verbose)
- `g` (global) and `y` (sticky) in JavaScript
- `u` (Unicode) in JavaScript
- `U` (ungreedy) in PCRE
- Inline modifiers `(?i)`, `(?m:...)`

**Goal:** Control engine behavior globally or locally.

+++

+++ #### Unicode & Advanced Character Handling

- Unicode properties `\p{L}`, `\p{N}`, `\p{Script=Greek}`
- `\X` (grapheme cluster)
- Case folding and Unicode case-insensitivity
- Line break conventions (`\r\n` vs. `\n`)
- Normalization issues (NFC, NFD)

**Goal:** Handle international text correctly.

+++

+++ #### Advanced Constructs

- Atomic groups `(?-->...)`
- Conditional patterns `(?(1)yes|no)`
- Recursion `(?R)`, `(?1)` (PCRE)
- Subroutines `(?&amp;name)`
- Branch reset `(?|...)`
- Inline comments `(?#...)` and free-spacing mode

**Goal:** Write powerful, recursive, and complex patterns.

+++

+++ #### Performance &amp; Debugging

- Backtracking mechanics (NFA vs. DFA engines)
- Catastrophic backtracking and how to avoid it
- Possessive quantifiers and atomic groups as remedies
- ReDoS (Regular Expression Denial of Service)
- Benchmarking and profiling
- Writing maintainable regex (comments, spacing, testing)

**Goal:** Write fast, safe regex that won't blow up.

+++

+++ #### Real-World Patterns (Applied Practice)

- Email validation (and why "perfect" email regex is a myth)
- URL/URI parsing
- Date/time formats (ISO 8601, etc.)
- Log file parsing
- CSV (and its limits)
- HTML/XML (and why you shouldn't)
- Password strength rules
- Tokenizing simple languages

**Goal:** Apply knowledge to common problems and know when *not* to use regex.

+++

+++ #### Language-Specific APIs

- **JavaScript:** `RegExp`, `match`, `matchAll`, `replace`, `split`, `exec`, lastIndex
- **Python:** `re`, `re.compile`, `findall`, `finditer`, `sub`, raw strings
- **PCRE (PHP, Perl, grep -P):** unique features
- **Go (RE2):** no backreferences, linear time
- **Java:** `Pattern`, `Matcher`
- **sed/awk/grep:** basic vs. extended regex (BRE vs. ERE)

**Goal:** Use regex idiomatically in your language.

+++

+++ #### Suggested Practice Resources

- **regex101.com** — debug with explanations
- **regexcrossword.com** — gamified learning
- **RegexOne**, **RegexLearn** — interactive basics
- **"Mastering Regular Expressions" by Jeffrey Friedl** — the definitive book
- **rexegg.com** — advanced reference

+++

+++ #### Milestone Projects

1. **Beginner:** Validate phone numbers, zip codes, hex colors
2. **Intermediate:** Log parser, markdown link extractor, CSV tokenizer
3. **Advanced:** Mini-template engine, JSON-ish tokenizer, simple regex-based lexer

